    <bpmn:process id="W_W3704" name="W3704. Refund, Reversal &amp; Return Leakage Monitoring" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Refund/reversal transaction stream; daily report
Frequency: Continuous + daily
Volume: ~0.04% return rate (profile §5 — the ~40/day AR-credit-memo canon); refunds across all channels
Owner: Revenue Assurance Lead / Loss Prevention
Participants: Revenue Assurance Lead, Customer Service (links to VS-13), Returns (links to VS-32), Store Ops (links to VS-07), POS/IT (links to VS-08), Loss Prevention (links to VS-23), Finance (links to VS-17.1), BI (links to VS-28.1)
Source: workflow W3704 — Refund, Reversal &amp; Return Leakage Monitoring</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3704_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3704_Lane1" name="Revenue Assurance Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3704_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3704_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3704_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3704_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3704_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3704_Start3" name="Refund/reversal transaction stream; daily report">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3704_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3704_Task4" name="Revenue Assurance Lead monitor refund/reversal integrity: verify every…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Revenue Assurance Lead monitor refund/reversal integrity: verify every refund/void/no-sale/cancel is backed by a valid original transaction and authorized, detect refunds to different tender, refunds without merchandise return, and excessive refund activity by cashier/store
Responsible (R): Revenue Assurance Lead / Customer Service / Loss Prevention
Accountable (A): Revenue Assurance Lead
Duration: Daily</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3704_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3704_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3704_Task5" name="Revenue Assurance Lead/Loss Prevention investigate refund/reversal fraud…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Revenue Assurance Lead/Loss Prevention investigate refund/reversal fraud: detect sweethearting (refund to accomplice), fabricated refunds, return fraud (return of stolen/not-purchased goods, Wardrobing), and void-abuse (links to VS-23 W841/W1336); escalate for investigation
Responsible (R): Revenue Assurance Lead / Loss Prevention
Accountable (A): Revenue Assurance Lead
Duration: Daily</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3704_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3704_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3704_Task6" name="Revenue Assurance Lead/Finance reconcile refund/reversal to GL: confirm refund…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Revenue Assurance Lead/Finance reconcile refund/reversal to GL: confirm refund liability and reversal accounting is accurate (links to VS-17.1), quantify refund-leakage (fraudulent/erroneous refunds), and report to loss prevention (links to VS-23), customer service (links to VS-13), and leak-detection (W3705)
Responsible (R): Revenue Assurance Lead / Finance / Loss Prevention
Accountable (A): Revenue Assurance Lead
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3704_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3704_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3704_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3704_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3704_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-584 (ensure controlled execution — Pricing, Promotion, Loyalty &amp; Payment Integrity Monitoring (PA-118.2).) | - operational: refund-integrity monitoring; operational: reconciliation
Owner: Revenue Assurance Lead / Loss Prevention</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
