    <bpmn:process id="W_W5543" name="W5543. Price-File Integrity Event Response &amp; Mass-Mispricing Rollback" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A bad price-file push is detected — POS/ESL/shelf-label prices deviating from the approved price master beyond threshold (W3697 monitoring alarm, a store&#x27;s shelf-label audit exception, a customer DTI complaint, or a margin-variance spike) — affecting &gt; 50 SKUs or &gt; 1 store
Frequency: Rare as a *mass* event; ~2–5 events/year chain-wide cross the threshold (single-SKU label errors are the W3697 daily-detection steady state, not this workflow)
Volume: 1 event × affected SKUs × affected stores × exposure duration (units sold in the mispriced window from POS data — the quantification base in Step 5); worst-case scenario: a master-to-store propagation error touching all 200 stores
Owner: Revenue Assurance Lead / Merchandising-Pricing
Participants: Merchandising Pricing Team (the W13 price-file execution canon owner), IT Platform (price-file pipeline ESB/integration), Store Operations (re-label execution via the W63 task channel), VP Legal / Compliance (RA 7581 Price Act / Consumer Act exposure), Customer Service (refund handling per W1622 tiers), Finance Controller (margin impact), DTI liaison (per W427 regulatory-desk pattern), Corporate Communications (if consumer-facing)
Source: workflow W5543 — Price-File Integrity Event Response &amp; Mass-Mispricing Rollback</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5543_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5543_Lane1" name="Revenue Assurance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5543_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5543_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5543_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5543_Lane2" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5543_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5543_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5543_Lane3" name="Merchandising Pricing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5543_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5543_Lane4" name="Customer Service">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5543_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5543_Lane5" name="IT">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5543_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5543_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5543_Start7" name="A bad price-file push is detected — POS/ESL/shelf-label prices deviating from the…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5543_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5543_Task8" name="Confirm &amp; contain">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Confirm &amp; contain: reproduce the deviation (staged vs master price comparison per SKU/store); localize the fault — master-data error, pipeline transform error, or store-sync failure; freeze further price-file pushes (change-control hold with IT) to stop propagating; scope the blast radius: SKUs × stores × window start (first affected push timestamp from the W13 file log)
Responsible (R): Revenue Assurance Analyst / IT
Accountable (A): Revenue Assurance Lead
Duration: 1–4 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5543_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5543_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5543_Task9" name="Exposure &amp; regulatory triage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Exposure &amp; regulatory triage: split the SKU set — overcharged vs undercharged vs SRP-mandated (RA 7581 list); VP Legal assesses DTI exposure (SRP violations are strict-liability notices even if accidental) and the conspicuous-error defense posture for undercharges; if a DTI complaint already arrived, the W658-pattern response desk opens with the corrected master and sync logs as exhibits
Responsible (R): VP Legal / Revenue Assurance
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 2–8 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5543_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5543_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5543_Task10" name="Rollback &amp; re-label sweep">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Rollback &amp; re-label sweep: corrected file executes through the W13 canon (approve → distribute → verify POS/ESL sync at canary stores, then chain-wide); Store Operations issues the re-label task via the W63 channel with priority order: SRP-mandated SKUs, promo-endcap zones, high-velocity SKUs, then the tail; completion confirmed per store (label-count vs SKU-count match)
Responsible (R): Merchandising Pricing / Store Operations
Accountable (A): Revenue Assurance Lead
Duration: 4–24 hrs depending on scope</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5543_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5543_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5543_Task11" name="Customer remediation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Customer remediation: overcharge window — refund the difference at the service desk on receipt/loyalty-lookup evidence (W1622 approval tiers; W1538 refund mechanics), proactive outreach for loyalty-identifiable purchasers, price-difference honor policy published if consumer-facing; undercharge window — no clawback beyond the conspicuous-error/legal posture Legal set in Step 2; goodwill points per the loyalty policy where brand damage occurred
Responsible (R): Customer Service / Store Managers
Accountable (A): Revenue Assurance Lead
Duration: 1–14 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5543_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5543_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5543_Task12" name="Financial quantification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Financial quantification: compute exposure = Σ (price delta × units sold in window) per SKU/store from POS data; classify overcharge refunds (liability set aside per Controller) vs undercharge margin leak (revenue-leakage register per the VS-118.1 framework); feed the leakage-recovery analytics (W118.3)
Responsible (R): Revenue Assurance Analyst / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): Revenue Assurance Lead
Duration: 2–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5543_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5543_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5543_Task13" name="Regulatory close-out">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Regulatory close-out: respond to any DTI notice within deadline — corrective-evidence pack (master price history, push logs, rollback timestamps, remediation totals); compliance visit handled per the W658 inspection-response pattern; follow-up undertakings tracked to closure
Responsible (R): VP Legal / Compliance
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: Per DTI deadline</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5543_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5543_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5543_Task14" name="Root-cause &amp; pipeline hardening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Root-cause &amp; pipeline hardening: post-mortem with IT and Merchandising — pre-push validation gate (master-vs-staged automated diff, zero-tolerance on SRP-mandated SKUs), canary-store push stage added to the W13 execution canon, W3697 alert thresholds tightened (mass-deviation detector: &gt; N SKUs deviating in one store-day); runbook updated; report to the revenue-assurance governance forum
Responsible (R): IT / Revenue Assurance / Merchandising
Accountable (A): Revenue Assurance Lead
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5543_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5543_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5543_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5543_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5543_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-584 (ensure controlled execution — Pricing, Promotion, Loyalty &amp; Payment Integrity Monitoring (PA-118.2).) | - operational: no chain-wide price-file push resumes after a mass-deviation event until the canary-store verification passes under the W13 canon | - operational: every confirmed overcharge window produces a quantified refund liability and a remediation register entry reviewed by the Controller
Owner: Revenue Assurance Lead / Merchandising-Pricing</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5543_Assoc17" sourceRef="W5543_Annotation16" targetRef="W5543_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
